ent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1143009A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations> </technical-data> <parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIGAWA TAKANORI</name> <address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>RIKEN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YABUKI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA SHIGEYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIGAWA, TAKANORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>RIKEN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUKI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA, SHIGEYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIGAWA TAKANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YABUKI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA SHIGEYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIGAWA, TAKANORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUKI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA, SHIGEYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing a polypeptide in a cell-free protein synthesis system with the use of dialysis, which comprises forming the polypeptide via the translation or transcription/translation of a nucleic acid encoding the polypeptide in the cell-free protein synthesis system containing a concentrated cell extract, and then taking up the polypeptide. By using this process, a desired polypeptide can be synthesized within a short period of time at a high yield and at a low cost, compared with the conventional processes.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé permettant de produire un polypeptide dans un système de synthèse protéique acellulaire, notamment grâce à l'utilisation de la dialyse. Ce procédé consiste tout d'abord à former le polypeptide par traduction ou transcription/traduction d'un acide nucléique codant pour ce polypeptide dans le système de synthèse protéique acellulaire, cet acide nucléique contenant un extrait cellulaire concentré, puis à reprendre ledit polypeptide. En employant ce procédé, on peut synthétiser le polypeptide souhaité dans un laps de temps limité, et ce pour un rendement plus élevé et des coûts inférieurs à ceux des procédés traditionnels.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>